Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>

Here is the root cause:
When auxiliary_device_add() fails, the error path calls auxiliary_device_uninit() which frees iadev via the release callback. The code then falls through to the next error label, which reads adev->id from the freed iadev for ida_free() and also calls kfree() on the already freed iadev, causing double free and use-after-free.

Here is the patch:
